{
  "requirement": "`Criterion::execute` can compute an answer without a configured model provider.\nA criterion can compute its answer directly using tracked inputs; deterministic\nexecution needs no configured agent. Evidence storage is still required.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.execution.deterministic_procedures`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `Criterion::execute` can compute an answer without a configured model provider.\n2. The criterion computes its answer directly from tracked inputs.\n3. Evidence storage is still required.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]`:\n  - It builds `Validator::new(graph.clone())` with no `with_agent`. `Validator::new` sets `agent: None` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/graph/runtime.rs#impl[Validator<D>]/fn[new]`.\n  - `Review::execute` reads the node contents through `ctx.inspection().read(...)`, which is the tracked-input path. The test asserts `result.output().rationale` equals \"ordinary computation\", so the answer was computed from that input and no agent was involved.\n  - It stores the evidence through the graph's storage, loads it back, and asserts that the saved `dependencies[0]` is `Dependency::Node(Node(1), fingerprint)` with the expected fingerprint value. This shows the tracked input was recorded.\n  - Evidence storage is exercised directly: the validator is constructed from the storage-providing `Memory` domain, and `store_evidence` and `load_evidence` are both used.\n- `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` and `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]`:\n  - Both run `verify` on a `Validator` that has no agent and assert the computed outputs. These cover more criteria, including typed outputs and a negative answer.\n  - The contracts test asserts that executions are counted and that stored records are written only on explicit save. The validation test asserts the stored records and their empty dependencies.\n\n**Storage requirement**\nThe storage requirement is structural: `Validator::new` takes the domain that provides evidence storage. The tests supply it and use it for the store and load round trips.\n\n**Gaps**\nI found no untested obligation and no relevant test that lacks a `{test}` marking. The requirement has no failure case or boundary that it names.",
